WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.270
So yesterday was Memorial Day here in the
United States.

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:11.040
Donald Trump was at a wreath laying ceremony
and I got a ton of emails and a bunch of articles

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:18.619
I read arguing that Donald Trump was visibly
struggling to stand at a Memorial Day event

00:00:18.619 --> 00:00:25.710
and that there is this sort of weird way in
which Trump seems to be off balance and regularly

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.990
recalibrating his balance.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.609
So I'm not going to spend a ton of time on
this.

00:00:30.609 --> 00:00:36.860
If you know my show, you know, we've covered
Trump's strange behavior, whose sources we've

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:38.340
never yet determined.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.410
We've not yet determined.

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:41.480
And I'm going to talk about that a little
bit.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:45.150
Let's let's first look at the videos and then
I'll tell you what I think.

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:49.850
Here is one video during a rendition yesterday
of the national anthem.

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:52.790
And Donald Trump does seem unable to just
stand up straight.

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:59.020
His whole upper torso is sort of rocking for
forward and back as he's in a salute position.

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:01.060
And it wasn't a windy day.

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.450
Reports are that wind was only four miles
per hour.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:05.930
No one else is swaying in that way.

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:08.190
And that was the source of some of the concern.

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:13.610
Here is another video from yesterday in which
Donald Trump walks up to a wreath and is staring

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:14.610
at it.

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:18.930
And again, he's kind of swaying in the wind,
sort of swaying back and forth.

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:23.270
And he does at moments seem like he's going
in the direction of falling over.

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:27.670
But his balance system realizes it and compensates
by pulling him back.

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:31.870
So I want to be like a hundred and ten percent
crystal clear.

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:34.450
This could be something or it could be nothing.

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:39.190
And we've seen we've seen this type of stuff
since day one with Trump.

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:45.240
These inner ear balance type issues can be
related to all sorts of different things in

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:51.660
earlier stages, sometimes even before other
dementia symptoms develop, starting to have

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:52.660
issues.

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:58.920
Balancing when standing or walking can suggest
an increased potential to develop Alzheimer's

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:01.450
or other types of dementia.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:06.030
Balance issues can be related to medications
side effects.

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:09.940
People speculate that Trump takes stimulants.

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:14.129
Stimulants can certainly affect your balance,
but they can also simply affect your ability

00:02:14.129 --> 00:02:19.569
to sit still because you're energized in this
way that uppers, stimulants and amphetamines

00:02:19.569 --> 00:02:21.519
can can do.

00:02:21.519 --> 00:02:23.810
This could also be Trump's weird stance.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:28.560
I know some of you are aware that Trump stands
in a very weird way, kind of hinged forward

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:32.540
at the at the hips that might make it difficult
to stand still.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:36.620
There's speculation that Trump stands that
way because he wears lifts in his shoes, which

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:39.239
sort of lean him forward.

00:02:39.239 --> 00:02:42.189
What we know is this is not new.

00:02:42.189 --> 00:02:44.659
What we know is it wasn't windy yesterday.

00:02:44.659 --> 00:02:46.719
Trump wasn't getting blown around by wind.

00:02:46.719 --> 00:02:52.209
So if you say to me, do I think something
is up here, big picture.

00:02:52.209 --> 00:02:54.060
You all know I think something's up.

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:58.269
And I don't know if the video from yesterday
is part of it or if it's something new or

00:02:58.269 --> 00:02:59.299
if it's nothing.

00:02:59.299 --> 00:03:01.430
If you say, do I really care?

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:06.349
Well, I care if it's something that's impacting
Trump's cognition because he's the president

00:03:06.349 --> 00:03:07.959
of the United States.

00:03:07.959 --> 00:03:15.150
Whether or not something like this explains
Trump's behaviors and actions, Trump has failed.

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:16.150
Either way.

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:17.150
Right.

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:19.989
Like the Corona virus response has been a
failed response.

00:03:19.989 --> 00:03:26.659
Whether Trump has dementia, an inner ear issue
is abusing drugs or whatever the case may

00:03:26.659 --> 00:03:27.659
be.

00:03:27.659 --> 00:03:28.749
It could be ADHD.

00:03:28.749 --> 00:03:29.749
Right.

00:03:29.749 --> 00:03:35.819
I mean, maybe Trump can stand still, but does
a good job because he has ADHD and it's hard

00:03:35.819 --> 00:03:37.230
for him to stand still.

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:38.230
Who cares?

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:39.230
Right.

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:41.680
The point is he's not doing a good job.

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:47.199
And he can't stand still and looks unstable
and looks confused and got off of Air Force

00:03:47.199 --> 00:03:52.170
One and didn't recognize his own limo in front
of him and wandered off until a Secret Service

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:55.029
agent brought him back holding him.

00:03:55.029 --> 00:03:57.040
Is that why he's a bad president?

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:58.040
No.

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:00.510
He'd be a terrible president no matter what
the explanation is.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:04.040
Does it aggravate the lethality of this presidency?

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:05.040
Yeah.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:06.040
Yeah.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:07.049
It probably does.

00:04:07.049 --> 00:04:10.010
Will we ever know what's really going on here?

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:11.010
I don't know.

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:16.930
I know inside the Reagan White House, they
knew while he was president that he was starting

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:20.120
to show signs and symptoms of Alzheimer's.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:24.450
It was learned sort of officially, publicly
later.

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:29.419
Only in retrospect did people start figuring
out that it was not something that happened

00:04:29.419 --> 00:04:31.570
only after he was out of office.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:34.289
He was experiencing symptoms while he was
in office.

00:04:34.289 --> 00:04:40.699
My instinct is we probably would not get anything
definitive about Trump while he is in office.

00:04:40.699 --> 00:04:45.990
It is yet another reason to get him out in
November, meaning he would leave in January

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:48.699
rather than giving him another four years.

00:04:48.699 --> 00:05:30.550
Hopefully someday we do know exactly what

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:46.669
it

00:05:46.669 --> 00:06:03.530
is

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:15.470
that is going on.

